    "intro_html":  "Swiss steak has nothing to do with Switzerland. The name comes from swissing, an old term for pounding tough meat until it gives up, and that is the whole idea here. Flour dredged beef braises in tomatoes, peppers, and onion until it cuts with a fork. No cream, no cheese, and not much fuss. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
